<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ice0c81fb887bd73af5c5541158865c2871cea09b" commit="7272c4142ccd2348aa83685a6b284e9437e6809e" commit_message="tast: Make bundle.Local support waiting for DUT readiness.  Make the bundle.Local function take an optional func that is executed to wait for the DUT to become ready for testing. This provides a mechanism that the local &quot;cros&quot; bundle can use to defer testing until critical Chrome OS system daemons are running.  BUG=chromium:897521 TEST=added unit tests; also manually verified (in      conjunction with tast-tests change) that ready function      runs and that testing doesn't start if debugd is      stopped CQ-DEEND=Ieb8536ad3adbe389a80614014772cf1e8d34db69  Change-Id: Ice0c81fb887bd73af5c5541158865c2871cea09b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1298595 Commit-Ready: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shuhei Takahashi &lt;nya@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hidehiko Abe &lt;hidehiko@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1298595" owner_email="derat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/tast" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/tast" ref="refs/changes/95/1298595/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ieb8536ad3adbe389a80614014772cf1e8d34db69" commit="287db8a50beb11811e86ca7b80c7791d65ecc42e" commit_message="tast-tests: Make local cros bundle wait for DUT to be ready.  Make the local &quot;cros&quot; test bundle wait for the system-services, debugd, and shill Upstart jobs to be running before tests are run.  BUG=chromium:897521 TEST=manual: verified that &quot;tast run&quot; waits for a stopped      debugd job before starting tests CQ-DEPEND=Ice0c81fb887bd73af5c5541158865c2871cea09b  Change-Id: Ieb8536ad3adbe389a80614014772cf1e8d34db69 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1298263 Commit-Ready: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shuhei Takahashi &lt;nya@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1298263" owner_email="derat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/tast-tests" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/tast-tests" ref="refs/changes/63/1298263/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib9ad4f5a8bc6ce88ffdcbafe2039fea8f5bc2e50" commit="bd586b4142a1c2a6860302df6cca9a56faf19b45" commit_message="biod: create a virtual input device.  Like any other input device, we need to reset idle and suspend timeouts on user interaction with the fingerprint sensor. Also we need powerd to supress wake interrupts if lid is closed. This patch adds functionality to create a virtual input device. Reporting user activity will be added in further CLs.  BUG=b:112974410 TEST=Test that a virtual input device is created.  Change-Id: Ib9ad4f5a8bc6ce88ffdcbafe2039fea8f5bc2e50 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1279402 Commit-Ready: Ravi Chandra Sadineni &lt;ravisadineni@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ravi Chandra Sadineni &lt;ravisadineni@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Norvez &lt;norvez@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ravi Chandra Sadineni &lt;ravisadineni@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1279402" owner_email="ravisadineni@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="17" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/02/1279402/17" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib3fa3a85049eebb6c780a433d99e1932d133b08a" commit="b1dec451908e9eab57fabec59551760426fec778" commit_message="power: recognize cros fingerprint and control wakeups.  This patch includes udev rules to identify fingerprint sensor based on the name. It then control wakeups from the fingerpri